    ("p", "Four preparation steps turn the file into the catalogue that the book service loads on its first start. Titles are cleaned of stray separators and spaces. Only the first two authors are kept. The ISBN is the ten-digit ISBN where present, otherwise the thirteen-digit one; where both are missing or the value repeats, the identifier GB-<book id> is used so that the unique constraint of the database holds. The dataset has no genre field, so the category column holds the publication era (before 1950, 1950 to 1999, 2000 to 2009, 2010 onwards). Goodbooks-10k describes books, not physical copies, so the number of copies per title (1 to 5) is generated from the book identifier by a fixed rule, which gives exactly 2,000 titles of each size and a total of " + f"{copies:,} copies. The ratings are not used by the application."),
